        "Examples of transferable skills include:\n- Sales conversations.\n- Customer research.\n- Copywriting.\n- Content production.\n- Project management.\n- Client communication.\n- Service delivery.\n- Team training.\n- Operational analysis.\nA result that depends mainly on timing, market movements, or an unusual external event may not be repeatable in the same way.\n6.2 The opportunity-switching audit\nBefore abandoning one path for another, ask:\n1. Have I given the current path enough deliberate practice?\n2. What evidence says the opportunity is not viable?\n3. Am I leaving because the model is weak or because the work has become uncomfortable?\n4. Does the new opportunity build on skills I already have?\n5. What are the downside risks?\n6. What would I need to learn before risking money?\n7. Can I test the new path without abandoning everything?\n6.3 Avoid copying a mentor's decisions blindly\nThe founder followed a mentor into crypto because the mentor appeared to be making substantial monthly income. The decision did not work out as hoped.",
